<sbb-container background-expanded color="white" class="lp-container no-margin-top">
  <sbb-title level="2" visual-level="2">What are skills?</sbb-title>

  <div class="roadmap-teaser">
    <sbb-card color="milk" class="sbb-card-spacing-l">
      <sbb-icon name="magic-wand-medium"></sbb-icon>
      <sbb-title level="3" visual-level="4">Skills.</sbb-title>
      <p class="subtext">Skills are abilities that extend GitHub Copilot with Lyne, the SBB icons and Figma. Your assistant then knows the SBB Design System and works with it.</p>
    </sbb-card>
    <sbb-card color="milk" class="sbb-card-spacing-l">
      <sbb-icon name="hammer-wrench-medium"></sbb-icon>
      <sbb-title level="3" visual-level="4">The toolkit.</sbb-title>
      <p class="subtext">The toolkit is the collection of these skills. You install it once on your computer.</p>
    </sbb-card>
    <sbb-card color="milk" class="sbb-card-spacing-l">
      <sbb-icon name="rocket-medium"></sbb-icon>
      <sbb-title level="3" visual-level="4">Your benefit.</sbb-title>
      <p class="subtext">With every update, you benefit from improvements and new skills. You update everything at once.</p>
    </sbb-card>
  </div>
</sbb-container>

<sbb-container background-expanded color="milk" class="lp-container">
  <sbb-title level="2" visual-level="2">What the skills can do.</sbb-title>
  <div class="sbb-grid-only lp-flipcards">
    <sbb-flip-card class="lp-flip-card-1">
      <sbb-flip-card-summary image-alignment="after">
        <sbb-title level="4">From idea to prototype.</sbb-title>
      </sbb-flip-card-summary>
      <sbb-flip-card-details>
        <sbb-title level="4" negative>From idea to prototype.</sbb-title>
        Describe in the chat what you need, and the assistant builds a clickable prototype from real Lyne components: in the SBB look, with dark mode and accessibility from the start. You quickly have something in your hands that you can show and discuss.
      </sbb-flip-card-details>
    </sbb-flip-card>
    <sbb-flip-card class="lp-flip-card-2">
      <sbb-flip-card-summary image-alignment="below">
        <sbb-title level="4">What you show can be built.</sbb-title>
      </sbb-flip-card-summary>
      <sbb-flip-card-details>
        <sbb-title level="4" negative>What you show can be built.</sbb-title>
        The AI knows the possibilities and the limits of Lyne. Your prototype therefore shows only what can also be implemented in development. The discussion «It works in Figma, so why not in development?» no longer applies.
      </sbb-flip-card-details>
    </sbb-flip-card>
    <sbb-flip-card class="lp-flip-card-3">
      <sbb-flip-card-summary image-alignment="below">
        <sbb-title level="4">Lyne-compliant from the first line.</sbb-title>
      </sbb-flip-card-summary>
      <sbb-flip-card-details>
        <sbb-title level="4" negative>Lyne-compliant from the first line.</sbb-title>
        The included starter sets up your project so that components, design tokens and themes are integrated correctly from the start. Your prototype stands on the same foundation as later products and does not have to be rebuilt first.
      </sbb-flip-card-details>
    </sbb-flip-card>
    <sbb-flip-card class="lp-flip-card-4">
      <sbb-flip-card-summary image-alignment="below">
        <sbb-title level="4">Your Figma designs, implemented.</sbb-title>
      </sbb-flip-card-summary>
      <sbb-flip-card-details>
        <sbb-title level="4" negative>Your Figma designs, implemented.</sbb-title>
        The assistant reads your Figma designs and implements them with Lyne components. You set up the connection once, and the onboarding guides you step by step. {# CONFIRM: scope of the Figma connection #}
      </sbb-flip-card-details>
    </sbb-flip-card>
  </div>
</sbb-container>

<sbb-container background-expanded color="white" class="lp-container">
  <sbb-title level="2" visual-level="2">Design Studio &amp; Skills.</sbb-title>
  <p class="sbb-text-m">Planning a design studio? This is where the skills play to their strengths. The sketching round stays as it is: quick and rough. Afterwards, you turn the favourites into clickable prototypes that you can test with users.</p>

  <div class="roadmap-teaser">
    <sbb-card color="milk" class="sbb-card-spacing-l">
      <sbb-icon name="pen-medium"></sbb-icon>
      <sbb-title level="4" visual-level="4">1. Sketch.</sbb-title>
      <p class="subtext">As usual: the team sketches many ideas quickly and roughly. The skills are deliberately not used here yet, so that the variety of ideas does not suffer.</p>
    </sbb-card>
    <sbb-card color="milk" class="sbb-card-spacing-l">
      <sbb-icon name="layers-medium"></sbb-icon>
      <sbb-title level="4" visual-level="4">2. Build prototypes.</sbb-title>
      <p class="subtext">From the two or three favourites, the skills create clickable prototypes from real Lyne components. They feel real and can be tested right away. {# CONFIRM: effort and scope per prototype #}</p>
    </sbb-card>
    <sbb-card color="milk" class="sbb-card-spacing-l">
      <sbb-icon name="hand-cursor-medium"></sbb-icon>
      <sbb-title level="4" visual-level="4">3. Test.</sbb-title>
      <p class="subtext">The prototypes go straight into testing with users. And because the prototypes are built with Lyne, you immediately see what can be implemented.</p>
    </sbb-card>
  </div>
</sbb-container>

<sbb-container background-expanded color="milk" class="lp-container">
  <div class="sbb-grid-only">
    <div class="inset">
      <sbb-title level="2" visual-level="2">Ready in 3 steps.</sbb-title>
      <ol class="sbb-step-list sbb-text-m" style="--sbb-background-color-3: var(--sbb-background-color-1);">
        <li>
          <strong>Prepare.</strong>
          <p class="subtext">You need the SBB network or VPN, a computer with macOS or Windows with WSL, and <sbb-link href="https://code.visualstudio.com/download" target="_blank">VS Code</sbb-link> with the <sbb-link href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=GitHub.copilot" target="_blank">GitHub Copilot</sbb-link> extension (on a Mac, alternatively the <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><sbb-link href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/get-started/quickstart-copilot-app" target="_blank">Copilot App</sbb-link>)</span> and <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><sbb-link href="https://nodejs.org/en/download" target="_blank">Node.js</sbb-link>.</span> Nothing else.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Install.</strong>
          <p class="subtext">The guide takes you step by step from zero to your first task. Allow about 30 minutes, and you do most steps only once per computer.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Get started.</strong>
          <p class="subtext">Write «Set up the UX toolkit.» in the chat and off you go: the assistant shows you what the skills can do and asks about Figma and a folder for your prototypes. {# CONFIRM: the English onboarding prompt #}</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <sbb-button-link href="https://code.sbb.ch/projects/KD_UX/repos/ux-toolkit/browse/docs/installation.en.md" target="_blank" size="m">Guide (SBB network/VPN only)</sbb-button-link>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</sbb-container>

<sbb-container background-expanded color="white" class="lp-container">
  <div class="sbb-grid-only">
    <div class="inset">
      <sbb-title level="2" visual-level="2">Frequently asked questions.</sbb-title>
      <sbb-accordion>
        <sbb-expansion-panel color="white">
          <sbb-expansion-panel-header>What are skills?</sbb-expansion-panel-header>
          <sbb-expansion-panel-content>Skills are abilities that extend GitHub Copilot with Lyne, the SBB icons and Figma. The toolkit bundles them: you install it once and benefit from all improvements and new skills.</sbb-expansion-panel-content>
        </sbb-expansion-panel>
        <sbb-expansion-panel color="white">
          <sbb-expansion-panel-header>Do I need programming skills?</sbb-expansion-panel-header>
          <sbb-expansion-panel-content>No, you do not need any programming skills at all. The assistant builds the prototypes for you, and the guide explains every installation step from scratch.</sbb-expansion-panel-content>
        </sbb-expansion-panel>
        <sbb-expansion-panel color="white">
          <sbb-expansion-panel-header>Do I need Figma?</sbb-expansion-panel-header>
          <sbb-expansion-panel-content>No, the Figma connection is optional. If you do not work with Figma, you skip this step.</sbb-expansion-panel-content>
        </sbb-expansion-panel>
        <sbb-expansion-panel color="white">
          <sbb-expansion-panel-header>Does the toolkit also run on Windows?</sbb-expansion-panel-header>
          <sbb-expansion-panel-content>Yes, on Windows it runs through WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux), not in PowerShell. The guide contains the matching steps.</sbb-expansion-panel-content>
        </sbb-expansion-panel>
        <sbb-expansion-panel color="white">
          <sbb-expansion-panel-header>What is the working folder?</sbb-expansion-panel-header>
          <sbb-expansion-panel-content>The working folder is the home of the toolkit on your computer. It contains the skills and defines which version is installed. The assistant only knows the skills if you open exactly this folder in VS Code or the Copilot App. Your prototypes are not stored in it but in a place you choose during onboarding. This way you can update the toolkit at any time without affecting existing prototypes.</sbb-expansion-panel-content>
        </sbb-expansion-panel>
        <sbb-expansion-panel color="white">
          <sbb-expansion-panel-header>Can the prototypes be used in production?</sbb-expansion-panel-header>
          <sbb-expansion-panel-content>Prototypes are made to show and align ideas, not for production use. {# CONFIRM #}</sbb-expansion-panel-content>
        </sbb-expansion-panel>
        <sbb-expansion-panel color="white">
          <sbb-expansion-panel-header>How do I stay up to date?</sbb-expansion-panel-header>
          <sbb-expansion-panel-content>For small updates, the assistant suggests them itself at the start of a session. For major updates, we will inform you. Prototypes remain unchanged.</sbb-expansion-panel-content>
        </sbb-expansion-panel>
        <sbb-expansion-panel color="white">
          <sbb-expansion-panel-header>Where do I give feedback?</sbb-expansion-panel-header>
          <sbb-expansion-panel-content>The assistant asks for it during onboarding. You can also <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><sbb-link href="mailto:ux@sbb.ch?subject=Skills%3A%20Feedback%20from%20FAQ">contact us directly</sbb-link>.</span></sbb-expansion-panel-content>
        </sbb-expansion-panel>
      </sbb-accordion>
    </div>
  </div>
</sbb-container>

